#!/usr/bin/env sh
# Easy Sales Export — pre-commit hook
#
# Runs lint-staged, which does two different things:
#
#   ESLint  --fix on the STAGED files only.
#   tsc     --noEmit over the WHOLE PROJECT, every time, whatever is staged.
#
# The second one is deliberate and cannot sensibly be narrowed. A type error is
# usually not in the file that caused it: change an interface here and the break
# appears in a caller you did not touch. Checking only staged files would miss
# exactly the errors worth catching.
#
# Cost, measured rather than assumed: about 5 seconds for tsc on this project,
# plus ESLint on whatever you staged.
#
# This is now the ONLY local type-check. .husky/pre-push used to run the same
# full tsc again before the unit suite; that duplicate has been removed, so the
# tree is checked here and then in CI, rather than three times.
#
# Which means the gap this hook cannot see matters more than it did. git does
# not run pre-commit for a merge commit, so merging two individually clean
# branches into a type-broken tree is not caught locally at all — CI catches it
# on the PR. If that ever proves too late, put the check back in pre-push
# rather than trying to widen this one.
npx lint-staged
